  "description": "A docfx plugin (and reusable library) that converts Jupyter Notebook (.ipynb) files into rendered documentation. Notebooks are claimed by a docfx IDocumentProcessor, converted to Markdown (markdown cells verbatim, code cells as fenced blocks, execution outputs as HTML, attachments inlined as base64 data URIs), and rendered through the docfx Markdown pipeline. The core NotebookConverter is also usable standalone.",
